    "result_text": "The suite contains only the acceptance test, and it's green. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented rejection of owner creation when the lower-cased email already belongs to another owner, responding with **409 Conflict**, following the existing patterns for the other duplicate/conflict rules.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`DuplicateOwnerEmailException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` carrying the offending email, mirroring `DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException`.\n\n2. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` mapping `DuplicateOwnerEmailException` to a 409 `ProblemDetail` with `errors: [\"email\"]`.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, after the email is normalized (lower-cased by `normalizeEmail`), it now checks `isDuplicateEmail(...)` and throws the new exception. The helper skips blank/absent emails (email is optional) and compares case-insensitively against every existing owner's email.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
